---Launch a configured change runner
---
---Starts the requested configured trail runner against the trail's current head. Repeating a request while that runner is active returns the existing run with outcome already_in_progress; outcome already_complete means a completed review already covers this head and nothing new launched. A run recorded failed at launch because its prompt is over the 64 KiB launch limit answers 422 with the message the run records. A launch refused for billing (the free trial is used up, a monthly spend limit was reached, or billing is suspended) also answers 422, with a message saying what to do next and a code naming the reason, and records no run. A runner that only declares the push trigger (not api) is refused with 409 unless its own latest run for this trail already failed, timed out, or was canceled — this route only ever retries a real prior failure for that runner, it never grants it unconditional manual launching — and that retry is scoped to native review runners (trails_review-enabled); a merged/closed trail or one with no valid head is refused with 422, matching review-rerun's own admission.
---
---`POST /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}/changes/{number}/runs/{runnerId}`
---@param input entire.trail_runs.LaunchChangeRunnerRequest
---@return entire.trail_runs.ManualTrailRunnerLaunchBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
